<title>USA: F.N.B. to trade on Nasdaq National Market.</title>
<headline>F.N.B. to trade on Nasdaq National Market.</headline>
<dateline>HERMITAGE, Pa. 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>F.N.B. Corp said Tuesday its common stock will begin trading on the Nasdaq National Market under the symbol &quot;FBAN&quot; on June 16.</p>
<p>The company's stock is currently traded on the Nasdaq SmallCap Market.</p>
<p>F.N.B., headquartered in Hermitage, Pennsylvania, is a bank holding company with $2.5 billion in assets that operates eight banks and a consumer finance subsidiary in Pennslyvania, Ohio, New York and Florida.</p>
